    description: "Found in DEEP bakeoff deep-20260623-134237 cohort-001 iter-004. The compact view (hg.4k/16k/64k) embeds FULL survey node objects (~23 fields each: id, name, kind, span, stable_id, shape_id, signature, docstring, meta, supply_chain, ...), so at a 4k or 16k token budget only ONE large symbol fits. Cohort evidence: apollo 4k=1/16k=1/64k=59 nodes; pretix 4k=1/16k=1/64k=83 (coverage 0.0001); spring 4k=1/16k=1 (all mvnw/pom build-file nodes). This single root cause produces THREE downstream failures the cohort flagged: (a) LOW_AVG_SLICE_NODES WARNs; (b) WI-kolal containment-monotonicity violation (4k picks a different single symbol than 16k -> 4k not subset of 16k, on apollo+pretix); (c) WI-zulij low centrality coverage (the 83 pretix nodes hold 1.3% of total centrality). FIX: the compact view should emit COMPACT node representations (id + name + kind + a couple key fields), not full survey nodes, so the token budget fits far more symbols. Closes/unblocks the WI-kolal and WI-zulij no_move verdicts. Repro: inspect hg.4k.json/hg.16k.json node counts on any large-symbol repo."  # 3841
    fields: {}  # 3841
