  message: "FIXED + CLOSED — PR de2fb3717c (merged to dev @ 29ddaa1ea3). Two changes: (1) new compact_node() slim projection (id/name/qualified_name/kind/language/path/span/signature/docstring + annotated centrality) used at every compact/tiered node-serialization site, dropping the ~200-byte supply_chain block + identity/provenance internals that cost ~250 tokens/node; (2) the tiered path now re-projects features[] onto the retained node set (before the shrink loop so the token estimate is accurate) instead of copying it wholesale — features[] was the real overhead (apollo's lone feature = ~25k tokens referencing thousands of nodes; since the shrink loop only removes nodes it stayed over budget no matter how many nodes were trimmed). BEHAVIORAL evidence (production format_tiered_behavior_map on real DEEP repo data, merged code): 4k/16k/64k node counts 1/1/59 -> 4/31/142 (apollo-server) and 1/1/83 -> 5/38/190 (pretix); apollo/spring tiers now containment-monotonic. compact.py 100% covered; full compact suite (195) + survey-level tests green. Found via DEEP bakeoff iter-004."  # fbc0
